    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it is true that combining sertraline with medications containing high doses of certain pain relievers like meperidine (Demerol) can trigger serotonin syndrome, standard dextromethorphan-based cough syrups typically do not pose this specific risk at typical doses. Dextromethorphan itself is a weak serotonin reuptake inhibitor, so mixing it with sertraline requires caution but is not strictly contraindicated for most people. Therefore, it is likely just an internet rumor exaggerated for dextromethorphan alone, but you should still take yourspecific symptoms notice and consult your pharmacist to confirm the ingredient list is safe for your case.",
